sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch14-14> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-14--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-14--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch14-14: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.39" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.393"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.5"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Some listed processes have ordinary dataset tests, and public sequences, occurrences and fossils speak to inheritance, distribution and extinction separately. The claim asserts that the whole list, taken together, produced living diversity, which is a program of research rather than one analysis. Discriminating power stays low because many different biological theories are compatible with the same broad list." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Treat the listed laws as separate variables, heritability, environmentally associated variation, population increase, differential persistence, divergence and extinction, and ask which of them can be shown jointly in existing datasets. The package is only partly testable: heritability, rapid potential increase and extinction have dataset criteria, while inheritance of use and disuse and the claim that this list jointly produces all living diversity do not have one decision rule." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The sentence binds several mechanisms, including variability from use and disuse, into one cause of all diversity, and those pieces do not share a single confirming result.", "Showing heritability or extinction in existing data leaves the joint production of the entangled bank untested.", "A small team cannot compile a decisive analysis of every named law from current databases in weeks." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-14--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-14--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-14--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-14--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch14-14 by Grok 4.7: 0.35" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.35"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-14--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch14-14> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-14--grok--operationalizability> .
